> > a) Reading: should Emacs move off the jj maildir for lab-devel? Or
> >    should the IMAP mirror sit beside it as a second notmuch profile? The
> >    patch workflow, process-email included, reads the jj maildir. If
> >    you move, your mail stops reaching the list through jj, so the
> >    moderated-delivery step in zib/patch-review-workflow.org changes.
>
> Yes this will switch from the jj maildir to synced maildir. I think it
> would be fine as a second profile, at least to start. Here's how I'd
> generally like the work to go (where each phase may have multiple
> commits if needed):
>
> 1. update to support lab-mail server
> 2. switch to lab-mail server config
> 3. clean up vestigial jj maildir

Thanks. The spec is posted as "[PATCH] dotfiles/notmuch: Spec reading
and sending through lab-mail" [1], in dotfiles/notmuch/spec.org. It
uses your three phases as its structure. Phase 1 adds a "lists"
notmuch profile, mbsync and msmtp config, the two packages, and
pat@p7x.dev as an allowed sender. Phase 1 changes nothing the jj
maildir client uses. Phase 2 points Emacs at the profile and sends
through msmtp. Phase 3 removes maildir-deliver.sh from dotfiles/emacs.

One finding sets the order, and the spec states it as a rule. Phase 2
lands only after process-email reads and sends through lab-mail too.
[inference] Once Emacs sends over SMTP, your mail no longer reaches
the jj maildir. I read only that maildir, so I would stop seeing your
mail, and my replies would stop reaching you. Moving process-email is
a separate spec, and I can write it next. Phase 1 does not depend on
it.

The profile's pre-new hook runs "mbsync lists", so a refresh in Emacs
fetches and indexes in one step. It needs no cron entry or daemon on
beastie. The spec lists a timer as the alternative if that turns out
to be slow.

> Let's go with pat@p7x.dev for the time being, just because it's already
> set up and I can verify the workflow.

Done. The spec lists "pat@p7x.dev is a sending identity on the Fastmail
account behind mail-creds" as a provider prerequisite. It also assumes
that mail to lab-devel@p7x.dev is filed into "lists" by your Fastmail
rule. [inference] I have not seen that address on lab-mail yet, since
the lab-mail acceptance test used lab@lists.p7x.dev. Step 1 of the
acceptance test checks it. Sending as pat@patmaddox.com is out of
scope. That replaces "[PATCH] todo: Send as Pat through lab-mail
later" [2], which I have dropped.

