The spec records this as accepted for now under "out of scope", and
it names the two fixes for later.

> I'm open to suggestions but I think this is a yes. Ultimately we should
> be able to restore the entire message status from the list data - but
> storing the message will mark it as sent right away, which is an over
> all lower latency process.

Agreed. Fcc goes to ~/mail/sent, beside the mirror and not inside it,
because mbsync owns ~/mail/lists. Tags still come only from the list's
contents. Acceptance step 7 checks your point: it rebuilds the
database and expects the same sent, inbox and replied tags.

I will start phase 1 once you approve the spec.

